mitk (2026.06-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging, ported from the neurofedora mitk.spec
    (2026.06-36) and built against system libraries (MITK_USE_SUPERBUILD=OFF):
    ITK 5.4, VTK 9.6, CTK with the plugin framework, ACVD, Qt 6, DCMTK,
    Boost, Poco and the rest of the Debian archive.
  * Ships mitk (module libraries), mitk-workbench (the BlueBerry Workbench
    and its plugins), mitk-dev (headers) and python3-mitk (pybind11
    bindings).
  * Patches 0001-0005 are carried over from the Fedora packaging (CTK
    component verification, test-driver target guard, missing <algorithm>,
    a GCC 16 ICE workaround, ITK's portable Eigen include spelling).
  * 0006: build against system libraries - stage the Python package in the
    build tree instead of the live site-packages, find ZLIB in module mode,
    VTK's LZ4::LZ4 target name, VTK 9.6's removal of vtkVectorOperators.h,
    guard Modules/PET's test dir behind BUILD_TESTING (it FetchContent-clones
    a dataset at configure time), and link ITKIODCMTK into MitkCore since
    Debian's ITK enables that IO factory.
  * 0007: distro install layout - do not run Qt's deploy tool (it exists to
    build a relocatable bundle and fails on system Qt), and install module
    libraries and headers, which upstream has no install rules for.
  * Deliberately unstripped: CppMicroServices appends resource archives to
    the module libraries and strip silently destroys them. Debug info is
    dropped at compile time instead.

 -- Morgan Hough <morgan.hough@gmail.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:43:15 -0700
